 "notes": "Combined ('Total') 95% CL exclusion contour for the joint Fermi-LAT analysis of 3C454.3, CTA 102 and 3C279 flares. Extracted programmatically from the white contour in Fig. 8 (lambda_tot heatmap, e-print file large_font_magma_white_ALL_nacuts_lambda_w_contour_COMB.png); identical to the thick black 'Total' contour in Fig. 9. Axes calibrated from major tick pixel positions (x: 10^1,10^2,10^3 neV; y: 10^-12..10^-10 GeV^-1, log-log). Curve is the lower boundary of the excluded region; it starts at the scan edge m_a=5 neV (g~7e-12), dips to ~4.6e-12 GeV^-1 near 12 neV, steps up sharply near 230 neV and terminates at the plot top (1e-10 GeV^-1) near 620 neV. Astrophysical (photon-ALP mixing in blazar jets) limit, independent of local DM density. Paper summary statement: excludes 5 neV < m_a < 200 neV, g > 5e-12 GeV^-1 at 95% CL.",
